From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:16:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] bluray: a BD-J playlist started again after its end plays
 again

A BD-J program that loops a menu's background clip waits for the end of
the playlist, then starts its player again. libbluray only set the rate
back to normal: the title stayed at its end, nothing more was read, and
the menu sat on its last picture with no button ever drawn.

A start from BD-J on a playlist read to its end now opens that playlist
again from its start, as a standalone player plays it again. A program
that selects another playlist, or seeks, before starting is unchanged:
either one leaves the title off its end.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/libbluray/bluray.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bluray.c b/src/libbluray/bluray.c
index 6a4a8a4..d20f9f5 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bluray.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/bluray.c
@@ -1294,6 +1294,8 @@ int bdpriv_sound_effect(BLURAY *bd, int id)
     return 0;
 }
 
+static int _open_playlist(BLURAY *bd, unsigned playlist, unsigned angle);
+
 void bdpriv_select_rate(BLURAY *bd, float rate, int reason)
 {
     if (reason == BDJ_PLAYBACK_STOP) {
@@ -1304,6 +1306,17 @@ void bdpriv_select_rate(BLURAY *bd, float rate, int reason)
     if (reason == BDJ_PLAYBACK_START) {
         /* playback is triggered by bdpriv_select_rate() */
         bd->bdj_wait_start = 0;
+
+        if (rate >= 0.5) {
+            bd_mutex_lock(&bd->mutex);
+            if (bd->title_type == title_bdj && bd->title && !bd->st0.clip &&
+                (bd->end_of_playlist & 1)) {
+                /* a playlist started again after its end plays again from its start */
+                BD_DEBUG(DBG_BLURAY, "bdpriv_select_rate(): restarting %s\n", bd->title->name);
+                _open_playlist(bd, atoi(bd->title->name), bd->title->angle);
+            }
+            bd_mutex_unlock(&bd->mutex);
+        }
     }
 
     if (rate < 0.5) {
